# Hebrew script integrity

Before sending any Hebrew reply, scan every Hebrew word (including text inside `[...]` tags).

## Hard rule

A Hebrew word may contain only Hebrew letters (U+05D0–U+05EA), niqqud, geresh/gershayim, and Hebrew punctuation. Never insert Latin letters (A–Z, a–z) inside a Hebrew word.

English is allowed only as **whole tokens**: `USERS`, `SQL`, `CREATE_TIME`, `DB-AM-04`.

## Required tags (copy exactly; all letters Hebrew)

`[קליטה]` `[אוטו]` `[חצי]` `[ידני]`

## Lookalikes — never substitute

| Latin | Do not use instead of |
|-------|------------------------|
| o / O | ו (vav) |
| i / I / l | י (yod) |
| n | נ or ן |
| c | ס |
| p | פ or ף |
| a | א |

## Proofread before send

If any Hebrew word contains a Latin letter, rewrite that word in Hebrew only, then send. Do not mention this check to the user.
